Time Complexity: O(n * log(sum(weights) - max(weights))), where n is the number of packages. We perform a binary search between the maximum single package weight and the sum of all weights, and for each candidate capacity we traverse all packages once to check feasibility.
Space Complexity: O(1), as we only use a few variables to track the current load and number of days. No additional data structures proportional to n are used.

